# Line endings (inspect with `git ls-files --eol`).
#
# Text is stored with LF. Files already committed with CRLF keep it: text=auto
# never converts a file whose committed version contains CR, so this rule
# rewrites nothing. It only stops editors and MinGW programs (which write CRLF
# to redirected stdout) from turning LF files into whole-file CRLF diffs.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated by `anyandroid compat --markdown > docs/compatibility/api-matrix.md`,
# whose output is CRLF: checked out with CRLF so that the file on disk is byte
# for byte the generator's output; stored with LF so that regenerating it never
# shows up as a whole-file diff.
docs/compatibility/api-matrix.md text eol=crlf
